# Recognizing Bias

#### Bias in AI doesn’t always appear as something obviously harmful or inappropriate. More often, it shows up in subtle ways—through assumptions, missing perspectives, or patterns in how information is presented.

#### To use AI responsibly, it’s important to recognize these patterns and consider how they might impact students and learning.

<div style="display:grid; gap:16px; max-width:90%; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; color:#292F36;">

<!-- Card 1 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/54bd64eab4eb2210b987f25a901674f9-Screenshot 2026-04-17 at 12.39.01 PM.png" 
     style="width:120px; height:120px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Relied on a stereotype</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI may repeat common but oversimplified ideas about groups of people.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Example:</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Describing certain jobs, behaviors, or abilities as typical for a specific gender, culture, or background.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Card 2 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/44b1d62deb6a8b4faab79151cd2d6e28-Screenshot 2026-04-17 at 12.39.05 PM.png" 
     style="width:120px; height:120px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Assumed one identity or experience</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI may present a single perspective as the “default” or “normal” experience.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Example:</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Assuming all students have the same home environment, cultural background, or access to resources.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Card 3 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/cbfdea16ccc1082fd69bfddcc21f5185-Screenshot 2026-04-17 at 12.39.08 PM.png" 
     style="width:120px; height:120px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Left out other perspectives</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI responses may ignore or minimize diverse viewpoints.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Example:</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Explaining a historical event from only one perspective without acknowledging others.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Card 4 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/4e96664d9d3798a6208d783662a216a7-Screenshot 2026-04-17 at 12.39.12 PM.png" 
     style="width:120px; height:120px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Language that isn’t inclusive</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI may use wording that unintentionally excludes or overlooks certain groups.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Example:</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Using terms or examples that don’t reflect the diversity of students in a classroom.
</div>
</div>
</div>

</div>


## What to Do When You Notice Bias

#### When something feels off, pause and reflect:
* #### Whose perspective is represented here?
* #### Whose perspective might be missing?
* #### What assumptions are being made?

>#### **💬 Quick Reflection:** What would you do if you recognized bias in an AI generated output?
